#: ../../../variable/CTEST_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY.rst:2
msgid "CTEST_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../variable/CTEST_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY.rst:6
msgid ""
"Specify the directory in which :manual:`ctest(1)` writes its output files in "
"a :ref:`Dashboard Client` script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../variable/CTEST_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY.rst:9
msgid ""
"CTest writes the files it produces during a run, such as the ``TAG`` file, "
"the logs under ``Temporary``, and the XML files submitted to a dashboard, "
"into a single output directory.  By default this is the ``Testing`` "
"directory under :variable:`CTEST_BINARY_DIRECTORY`.  Set this variable "
"before calling :command:`ctest_start` to write them elsewhere; the path may "
"be outside the build tree, and a relative path is interpreted with respect "
"to :variable:`CTEST_BINARY_DIRECTORY`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../variable/CTEST_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY.rst:17
msgid ""
"This makes it possible to run more than one :program:`ctest` process against "
"the same build tree, for example to run different subsets of the tests with "
"the ``INCLUDE_FROM_FILE`` option of :command:`ctest_test`, without the "
"processes overwriting each other's output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../variable/CTEST_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY.rst:22
msgid ""
"Outside of a dashboard script, use the :option:`ctest --output-dir` option."
msgstr ""
